# React architecture

## Data ownership

| Layer | Role |
|-------|------|
| **Server-state library** (React Query / TanStack Query) | Source of truth for remote data |
| **Realtime** (WebSocket, Centrifugo, SSE, …) | Sync / invalidation signal only — never the confirmation of a local user command |
| **React context / providers** | UI, auth session, and small ambient context (e.g. active tenant id) — **not** entity lists or caches of API resources |

Never store the same remote resource in both a provider and the query cache.

## User actions vs realtime

```
Current-user action (create / update / switch context)
  → HTTP (or RPC) mutation — response is source of truth
  → update cache immediately (setQueryData / invalidate / fetchQuery)
  → UI reflects server state

Event from elsewhere (other tab, other user, async job)
  → realtime handler
  → targeted invalidateQueries (or setQueryData if payload is complete)
```

**Do not** wait for a realtime event before refreshing after the current user's own mutation.

Invalidate the **narrowest** query keys needed (lists vs detail). Avoid broad prefixes that refetch unrelated detail queries.

## Query keys

- Centralize keys in one module (`queryKeys`)
- Nest by resource and scope (tenant / parent id when relevant)
- Same key + same hook in multiple components ⇒ shared cache, one network call

```ts
// Pattern
resource.all
resource.lists() / resource.list(filters?)
resource.detail(id)
resource.child.all(parentId)   // scoped under parent when multi-tenant
```

## API access from the browser

- Call an app-owned layer (BFF `/api/...`, SDK, or typed client) — not raw backend URLs sprinkled in components
- Keep `api.ts` + `hooks.ts` + `types.ts` per domain under `lib/` (or equivalent)
- Components consume hooks; they do not own fetch/error plumbing

## Realtime client

- Connect only when authenticated / when the feature needs it
- Failure to connect = quiet degrade (app stays usable via HTTP)
- Handlers: map event → cache update. No domain workflows inside the socket callback beyond that

## Components

- **Do not** define nested functions that return JSX inside a large component file
- Split UI into **small components in folders**; the parent only composes and wires hooks
- Colocate feature UI under a folder; put shared primitives in `components/ui/` (or design-system)

```
components/feature-name/
  index.tsx                 # composition + data hooks
  feature-header.tsx
  feature-list.tsx
  feature-form.tsx
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
function Page() {
  function renderHeader() { return <header>...</header> }
  function renderList() { return <ul>...</ul> }
  return <>{renderHeader()}{renderList()}</>
}

// ✅ GOOD
function Page() {
  return (
    <>
      <FeatureHeader />
      <FeatureList />
    </>
  )
}
```

- Logic reused across UI → custom hooks (`use-*.ts`), not inline in presentational files
- Code, comments, and identifiers in English
